WEBVTT

1
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.430
You're wearing a black cloak again.

2
00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.200
I've been sent to negotiate with you.

3
00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.820
It appears my trusting nature

4
00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:55.820
got the better of me.

5
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.190
It's happened before.

6
00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.860
I was hoping your loyalty was real

7
00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.860
when you pledged yourself to us. Jon Snow.

8
00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.700
Truly. I was.

9
00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:05.570
The Halfhand ordered me to join your army

10
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.370
and bring back whatever information

11
00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.370
I could to Castle Black.

12
00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.910
He made me kill him so you'd trust me.

13
00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.610
I was loyal

14
00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.120
to him and to my Night's Watch vows.

15
00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:16.980
All your vows?

16
00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.990
She wasn't enough to turn you. eh?

17
00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.060
Were you enough to turn her?

18
00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.790
She put three arrows in me when I escaped.

19
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.530
Did you see her again at Castle Black?

20
00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.060
Yes.

21
00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.730
And?

22
00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:38.830
She's dead.

23
00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.170
Your doing?

24
00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.140
No.

25
00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.780
We'll drink to her.

26
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.670
Of all the ways I'd kill you.

27
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.670
poison would be the last.

28
00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:20.410
- Ygritte.

29
00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:30.950
That's not wine.

30
00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:34.000
No. it's a proper northern drink. Jon Snow.

31
00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.320
You did well. Fought hard.

32
00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:40.160
Killed some of our strongest men.

33
00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.800
One of our giants went into your tunnel

34
00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.800
and never came out again.

35
00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:46.310
Mag the Mighty.

36
00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.340
He's dead.

37
00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:50.600
He killed my friend Grenn.

38
00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.010
He was their king.

39
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.920
The last of a bloodline that stretches back

40
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.920
before the First Men.

41
00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.450
Grenn came from a farm.

42
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.590
- Mag and Grenn.

43
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.590
- Grenn and Mag.

44
00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.130
Kullback. could I trouble you

45
00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.130
for something to eat?

46
00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.760
I don't imagine our guest has eaten anything

47
00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:15.760
for quite some time.

48
00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:21.100
So. you're here to strike a bargain?

49
00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:24.940
Turn your army around and go home.

50
00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.850
You know I know you're low on arrows.

51
00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.310
you're low on oil. you're low on men.

52
00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:31.180
How many are left. 50?

53
00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.550
I told Tormund and Orell.

54
00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:35.110
We have more than 1.000 men.

55
00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.650
I showed you everything I had.

56
00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.650
The whole army. 100.000 strong.

57
00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.290
And what did you do?

58
00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:42.290
You fired on us with everything you had.

59
00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.460
It wasn't much.

60
00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:47.990
As soon as I saw that.

61
00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:47.990
I sent 400 men to climb the Wall.

62
00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.560
an unmanned stretch five miles west of here.

63
00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:52.300
A lot of them will die climbing.

64
00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.470
but most of them will be over

65
00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.470
by the end of the day.

66
00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:00.170
It's me being honest with you. Jon Snow.

67
00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:00.170
which is more than you've ever done for me.

68
00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.650
My people have bled enough.

69
00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.840
We're not here to conquer.

70
00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:08.080
We're here to hide behind your Wall.

71
00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:08.080
Just like you.

72
00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.550
We need your tunnel.

73
00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.790
Now we both know that winter is coming.

74
00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:18.100
And if my people aren't south of the Wall

75
00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:18.100
when it comes in earnest.

76
00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.000
we'll all end up worse than dead.

77
00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.740
You want to strike a bargain with me?

78
00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.740
Here's the bargain.

79
00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.900
You go back. you open the gates to us.

80
00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.310
and I swear to you that no one else will die.

81
00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.570
Refuse.

82
00:07:32.650 --> 00:07:35.210
and we'll kill every last man at Castle Black.

83
00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.450
That's why you're here.

84
00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.560
I reckon you could do it

85
00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.560
before any of them could stop you.

86
00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.400
They'd kill you. of course.

87
00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:52.700
They'd kill you slow.

88
00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:56.470
But you knew that when you came in here.

89
00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:00.770
Are you capable of that. Jon Snow?

90
00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.280
Killing a man in his own tent

91
00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.280
when he's just offered you peace?

92
00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.180
Is that what the Night's Watch is?

93
00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.210
Is that what you are?

94
00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:12.440
Riders coming!

95
00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.620
- Are you attacking us?

96
00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.620
- No.

97
00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:19.250
It's like you said. we don't have the men.

98
00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.420
Hold! To me! To me!

99
00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.920
Stand down!

100
00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.960
I said my people have bled enough.

101
00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.070
and I meant it.

102
00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:44.900
Round them up.

103
00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.530
Stay with the horses.

104
00:10:56.750 --> 00:10:58.450
You're the King-beyond-the-Wall?

105
00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.990
- Do you know who I am?

106
00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.990
- Never had the pleasure.

107
00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:07.090
This is Stannis Baratheon.

108
00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:07.090
the one true king of the Seven Kingdoms.

109
00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.030
We're not in the Seven Kingdoms.

110
00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.030
and you're not dressed for this weather.

111
00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:14.470
It is customary to kneel

112
00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:14.470
when surrendering to a king.

113
00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.070
We do not kneel.

114
00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.010
I'll have thousands of your men

115
00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.010
in chains by nightfall.

116
00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.670
have nowhere to put them.

117
00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:27.670
have nothing to feed them.

118
00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.880
I'm not here to slaughter beat dogs.

119
00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:34.480
Their fate depends on their king.

120
00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.550
All the same. we do not kneel.

121
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.590
Take these men away.

122
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.200
What's a man of the Night's Watch

123
00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.200
doing in a wildling camp?

124
00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.830
I was sent to discuss terms

125
00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.830
with the King-beyond-the-Wall.

126
00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.270
You're speaking to the one true king. boy.

127
00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.140
You will address him as "Your Grace."

128
00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.200
I know he's the king. My father died for him.

129
00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.110
My name is Jon Snow. Your Grace.

130
00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.220
I'm Ned Stark's son.

131
00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:10.380
Your father was an honorable man.

132
00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:12.360
He was. Your Grace.

133
00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:14.330
What do you think he'd have done with him?

134
00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:23.360
I was this man's prisoner once.

135
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:26.530
He could have tortured me.

136
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:26.530
He could have killed me.

137
00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.670
But he spared my life.

138
00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.980
I think my father would

139
00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.980
have taken him prisoner.

140
00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:33.740
listened to what he had to say.

141
00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.820
Very well. then. Take him.

142
00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.080
Your Grace.

143
00:12:48.260 --> 00:12:50.890
If my father had seen the things that I've seen.

144
00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.870
he'd also tell you to

145
00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:54.870
burn the dead before nightfall.

146
00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:56.970
All of them.

147
00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.540
I would suggest milk of the poppy

148
00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.540
to ease his pain.

149
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.420
- but he is completely insensate.

150
00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.420
- Bloody Martells.

151
00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.720
The cause appears to be manticore venom.

152
00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.820
It is. The Death's Head manticore.

153
00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:22.860
I've read a great deal about it.

154
00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:22.860
It's a horrible poison.

155
00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.460
Usually Mantari in origin.

156
00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:28.860
There's nothing to be done.

157
00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.130
Yes. there is.

158
00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.730
May I ask what you think you're doing?

159
00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:35.870
Saving him.

160
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:40.510
Your Grace. I wish it were otherwise.

161
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:40.510
but Ser Gregor is beyond saving.

162
00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:43.110
Well. well beyond.

163
00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:47.620
This man is not even a maester.

164
00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:47.620
let alone grand maester.

165
00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.780
That's for the best.

166
00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.780
No maester knows how to save him.

167
00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:53.020
That is exactly the sort of arrogance

168
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.930
that had him expelled

169
00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:55.930
from the Citadel. Your Grace.

170
00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:00.300
His curiosity was deemed

171
00:13:56.000 --> 00:14:00.300
dangerous and unnatural.

172
00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.060
Rightly so. in my opinion.

173
00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.400
You're dismissed. Grand Maester.

174
00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:10.170
But. Your Grace. this is my laboratory.

175
00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.980
- Not anymore.

176
00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.980
- But...

177
00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.680
- You can save him?

178
00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:22.680
- Difficult to say. Your Grace.

179
00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:25.120
But if my past work is any guide.

180
00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:28.790
we stand a chance.

181
00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.300
Do everything you can.

182
00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.060
Come to me for anything you need.

183
00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:34.690
Thank you. Your Grace.

184
00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.540
You should know.

185
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:39.800
the process may change him

186
00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.270
somewhat.

187
00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:46.750
Will it weaken him?

188
00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:49.570
Oh. no.

189
00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:51.750
Very well. then.

190
00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.040
Not another word.

191
00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:14.870
We've been over this. The matter's closed.

192
00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:16.500
I'm opening it again.

193
00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.240
You were betrothed to Loras Tyrell.

194
00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.310
You're still betrothed to Loras Tyrell.

195
00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:28.020
And you will marry Loras Tyrell

196
00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:28.020
as soon as Tommen marries Margaery.

197
00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:29.220
I will not.

198
00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:32.280
Jaime cannot marry or inherit lands.

199
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.230
Tyrion's sentence

200
00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.230
will be carried out tomorrow.

201
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.930
You have on several occasions

202
00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:40.930
made great claims

203
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.770
about your commitment

204
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.770
to this family's future.

205
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.400
Your role in that future

206
00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:47.400
is more vital now than it ever was.

207
00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.380
I don't care.

208
00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.850
I will stay in King's Landing where I belong

209
00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.850
with my son. the king.

210
00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:56.580
When you were nine years old.

211
00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:56.580
I was called to the capital.

212
00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.920
I decided to take your brother with me

213
00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.920
and not you.

214
00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:04.220
You insisted that you would not be left

215
00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:04.220
at Casterly Rock under any circumstances.

216
00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.990
- If you recall...

217
00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.990
- I'm not interested in hearing

218
00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.620
another one of your smug stories

219
00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:09.620
about the time you won.

220
00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.960
This isn't going to be one of those times.

221
00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.660
Do you think you'll be the first person

222
00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:16.760
dragged into a Sept

223
00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:16.760
to be married against her will?

224
00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:18.670
When you marched into the throne room

225
00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:18.670
to tell me

226
00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.830
we'd won the Battle of Blackwater.

227
00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.830
do you remember?

228
00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:26.110
I was sitting on the Iron Throne with Tommen.

229
00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.170
I was about to give him

230
00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:28.170
essence of nightshade.

231
00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.720
That's how far I was willing to go

232
00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.690
when I thought someone awful

233
00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:32.690
had come to take my son away.

234
00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.250
Someone awful is coming to take him away.

235
00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:38.680
No.

236
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.790
Joffrey is dead.

237
00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.790
Myrcella's been sold like livestock.

238
00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.990
And now you want to ship me off

239
00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.990
to Highgarden and steal my boy.

240
00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:46.930
My last boy.

241
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.600
Margaery will dig her claws in.

242
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:50.600
you will dig your claws in.

243
00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:54.230
and you'll fight over him like beasts

244
00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:54.230
until you rip him apart.

245
00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:58.340
I will burn our house to the ground

246
00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:58.340
before I let that happen.

247
00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.350
And how will you do that?

248
00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.880
I'll tell everyone the truth.

249
00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.250
What truth would that be?

250
00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.150
You don't know. do you?

251
00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:17.030
You never believed it.

252
00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:18.790
How is that possible?

253
00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:24.370
What am I saying? Of course it's possible.

254
00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.840
How can someone so consumed

255
00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.840
by the idea of his family

256
00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:31.110
have any conception

257
00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:31.110
what his actual family was doing?

258
00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:35.250
We were right there in front of you.

259
00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:35.250
and you didn't see us.

260
00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.550
One real look in the past 20 years

261
00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.320
at your own children

262
00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.320
and you would have known.

263
00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.880
Known what?

264
00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:45.350
Everything they say is true

265
00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.990
- about Jaime and me.

266
00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.990
- No.

267
00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.790
- Your legacy is a lie.

268
00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.790
- No. no. no. no.

269
00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.890
I don't believe you.

270
00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:57.540
Yes. you do.

271
00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.420
Jaime.

272
00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:20.030
You won.

273
00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:22.790
One fewer brother. Must be proud of yourself.

274
00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:25.090
There's really nothing

275
00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:25.090
you wouldn't do. is there?

276
00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.030
For my family. no. nothing.

277
00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.160
I would do things for my family

278
00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.160
you couldn't imagine.

279
00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.830
- Tyrion is your family.

280
00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.830
- He's not.

281
00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.810
- You don't get to choose.

282
00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.810
- I do. So do you.

283
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.910
You can choose the creature that

284
00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.910
killed our mother to come into this world...

285
00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.450
Are you really mad enough

286
00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.450
to blame him for that?

287
00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:43.180
He didn't decide to kill her. He was an infant.

288
00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:45.080
A disease doesn't decide to kill you.

289
00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:47.820
All the same. you cut it out before it does.

290
00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:49.780
What do you decide?

291
00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.490
- What do you choose?

292
00:18:50.290 --> 00:18:52.490
- The things I did to get back to you.

293
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.050
to endure all that. only to find you...

294
00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.130
I choose you.

295
00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.100
- Those are words.

296
00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.100
- Yes.

297
00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:04.130
Like the ones I just said to Father.

298
00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.170
I told him.

299
00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:08.970
Told him what?

300
00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.810
I told him about us.

301
00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.980
- You told him?

302
00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.980
- I told him I won't marry Loras Tyrell.

303
00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.610
I told him I'm staying right here

304
00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.610
with Tommen. with you.

305
00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.490
- You think he'll just accept that?

306
00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:22.490
- Go and ask him.

307
00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:26.950
What did you say?

308
00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.290
I don't want to talk about Tywin Lannister.

309
00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.960
I don't choose Tywin Lannister.

310
00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:36.230
I don't love Tywin Lannister.

311
00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:36.230
I love my brother.

312
00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.670
I love my lover.

313
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:42.740
People will whisper. they'll make their jokes.

314
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:42.740
Let them.

315
00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.780
They're all so small. I can't even see them.

316
00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:48.010
I only see what matters.

317
00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:59.690
- Someone will walk in.

318
00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:59.690
- I don't care.

319
00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:11.230
You stand before Daenerys Stormborn.

320
00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.530
the Unburnt.

321
00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:13.970
Queen of Meereen.

322
00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.980
Queen of the Andals and the Rhoynar

323
00:20:14.610 --> 00:20:17.980
and the First Men.

324
00:20:18.810 --> 00:20:21.280
Khaleesi of the Great Grass Sea.

325
00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:24.650
Breaker of Chains and Mother of Dragons.

326
00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:31.660
Thank you for seeing me. Your Grace.

327
00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.700
My name is Fennesz.

328
00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.230
I can speak the Common Tongue. if you wish.

329
00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.060
You speak it very well.

330
00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:44.970
Before you freed me.

331
00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:44.970
I belonged to Master Mighdal.

332
00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:49.200
I was tutor to his children.

333
00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:49.200
I taught them languages and history.

334
00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:53.250
They know a great deal about your family

335
00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:53.250
because of me.

336
00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:58.750
Little Calla is only seven.

337
00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:58.750
but she admires you very much.

338
00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.720
I hope I can prove worthy of her admiration.

339
00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:03.720
What can I do for you?

340
00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:09.690
When you took the city. the children

341
00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:09.690
begged me not to leave the house.

342
00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.900
But Master Mighdal and I agreed that I must.

343
00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:16.770
So I lost my home.

344
00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:20.810
Now I live on the streets.

345
00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.570
I have outfitted mess halls

346
00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:25.040
to feed all former slaves

347
00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:25.040
and barracks to shelter them.

348
00:21:25.110 --> 00:21:27.410
I do not mean to offend. Your Grace.

349
00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:30.340
I went to one of these places.

350
00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:33.290
The young prey on the old.

351
00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.950
take what they want and beat us if we resist.

352
00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.360
My Unsullied will make them safe again

353
00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.360
in short order. my friend.

354
00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.660
this I promise you.

355
00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:44.500
Even if they are safe. who would I be there?

356
00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:47.330
What purpose would I serve?

357
00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.800
With my master. I was a teacher.

358
00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:54.500
I had the respect and love of his children.

359
00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:56.670
What is it that you want from me?

360
00:21:56.740 --> 00:21:58.370
Your Grace.

361
00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:02.640
I ask you to let me sell myself

362
00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:02.640
back to Master Mighdal.

363
00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:05.310
You want to return to a man who owned you

364
00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:07.750
like a goat or a chair?

365
00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:09.380
Please. Your Grace.

366
00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:12.690
The young may rejoice in the new world

367
00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:12.690
you have built for them.

368
00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.730
but for those of us too old to change.

369
00:22:15.800 --> 00:22:19.820
there is only fear and squalor.

370
00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:22.130
I am not alone.

371
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:26.070
There are many outside

372
00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:26.070
waiting to beg the same of you.

373
00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:30.870
I did not take this city to preside over

374
00:22:26.140 --> 00:22:30.870
the injustice I fought to destroy.

375
00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:33.610
I took it to bring people freedom.

376
00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:37.310
But freedom means making your own choices.

377
00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:41.820
I will allow you to sign a contract

378
00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:41.820
with your former master.

379
00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:45.290
It may not cover a period

380
00:22:41.920 --> 00:22:45.290
lasting longer than a year.

381
00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:47.390
Thank you. Your Grace.

382
00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:51.090
Thank you.

383
00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:58.930
The masters will take advantage

384
00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:58.930
of this situation.

385
00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:05.110
The men serving them

386
00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:05.110
will be slaves in all but name.

387
00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:13.250
Approach. my friend.

388
00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:21.120
I do not understand. my Queen.

389
00:23:23.960 --> 00:23:25.520
I do not understand. my Queen.

390
00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:27.730
The Queen says you may approach.

391
00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:40.080
I have brought you...

392
00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:46.190
He came from the sky.

393
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:50.420
The black one.

394
00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:55.830
The winged shadow.

395
00:23:57.560 --> 00:23:58.960
He came from the sky and...

396
00:24:05.110 --> 00:24:06.600
My girl.

397
00:24:07.780 --> 00:24:08.900
My little girl.

398
00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:15.340
What was her name?

399
00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:17.270
Zala. Your Grace.

400
00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:20.480
- How old was she?

401
00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:20.480
- Three.

402
00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:23.590
Three.

403
00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:27.690
And still no word of Drogon?

404
00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:34.130
Sailors saw him flying over the Black Cliffs

405
00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:34.130
three days ago. my Queen.

406
00:24:35.170 --> 00:24:36.540
Nothing since then.

407
00:24:39.670 --> 00:24:42.010
Meet me at the catacombs.

408
00:27:11.190 --> 00:27:15.530
They came to us

409
00:27:11.190 --> 00:27:15.530
from White Harbor and Barrowton.

410
00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:19.620
from Fairmarket and King's Landing.

411
00:27:19.700 --> 00:27:21.670
from north and south.

412
00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:23.830
from east and west.

413
00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:26.870
They died

414
00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:31.740
protecting men. women. and children

415
00:27:26.940 --> 00:27:31.740
who will never know their names.

416
00:27:31.850 --> 00:27:34.470
It is for us to remember them.

417
00:27:34.550 --> 00:27:36.280
Our brothers.

418
00:27:36.350 --> 00:27:39.380
we shall never see their like again.

419
00:27:39.450 --> 00:27:42.510
And now their watch is ended.

420
00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:47.030
And now their watch is ended.

421
00:28:58.630 --> 00:29:01.360
Your old blind man patched me up.

422
00:29:01.870 --> 00:29:02.860
Why?

423
00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:06.240
He's sworn to treat all wounded men.

424
00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:06.240
friend or foe.

425
00:29:06.310 --> 00:29:08.500
You want me alive so you can torture me?

426
00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:09.870
No one's gonna torture you.

427
00:29:09.940 --> 00:29:13.780
So how do we die? Hanging? Beheading?

428
00:29:14.210 --> 00:29:15.770
Drop us from the top of the Wall?

429
00:29:15.850 --> 00:29:17.840
I don't know what happens to the prisoners.

430
00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:19.750
Who decides?

431
00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:22.380
I suppose Stannis does.

432
00:29:23.090 --> 00:29:24.680
He your king now?

433
00:29:25.130 --> 00:29:26.960
I don't have a king.

434
00:29:28.300 --> 00:29:31.960
You spent too much time with us. Jon Snow.

435
00:29:32.770 --> 00:29:34.700
You can never be a kneeler again.

436
00:29:35.570 --> 00:29:38.040
We're gonna burn the bodies of your dead.

437
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:43.910
- Do you want to say any words over them?

438
00:29:39.640 --> 00:29:43.910
- Words? What kind of words?

439
00:29:43.980 --> 00:29:47.140
Funeral words.

440
00:29:43.980 --> 00:29:47.140
I don't know how the free folk do it.

441
00:29:47.210 --> 00:29:48.340
Do what?

442
00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:50.580
Say farewell.

443
00:29:51.820 --> 00:29:54.520
The dead can't hear us. boy.

444
00:29:59.590 --> 00:30:00.580
Snow.

445
00:30:05.430 --> 00:30:06.760
Did you love her?

446
00:30:10.040 --> 00:30:11.840
She loved you.

447
00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:15.370
- She told you?

448
00:30:12.840 --> 00:30:15.370
- No.

449
00:30:15.780 --> 00:30:18.540
All she ever talked about was killing you.

450
00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:20.740
That's how I know.

451
00:30:23.580 --> 00:30:25.780
She belongs in the North.

452
00:30:26.920 --> 00:30:28.650
The real North.

453
00:30:30.420 --> 00:30:32.050
You understand me?

454
00:32:17.960 --> 00:32:19.460
We can stop. We can rest.

455
00:32:19.530 --> 00:32:21.700
We'll rest with the three-eyed raven.

456
00:32:32.510 --> 00:32:34.480
We're not going to make it.

457
00:32:38.920 --> 00:32:40.390
We're already here.

458
00:32:40.450 --> 00:32:41.650
Jojen.

459
00:32:43.560 --> 00:32:44.890
Jojen.

460
00:32:45.490 --> 00:32:47.480
Look. Jojen.

461
00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:11.410
Jojen! Come on!

462
00:34:11.550 --> 00:34:13.740
Help them! Now!

463
00:34:14.110 --> 00:34:15.240
Hold on to me!

464
00:34:19.890 --> 00:34:20.980
Hang on!

465
00:34:23.220 --> 00:34:25.620
- Hodor. Hodor.

466
00:34:23.220 --> 00:34:25.620
- Help them!

467
00:34:26.060 --> 00:34:27.220
Hodor.

468
00:34:30.600 --> 00:34:31.860
Hodor!

469
00:34:48.110 --> 00:34:49.710
Hodor!

470
00:35:09.340 --> 00:35:10.430
Hodor.

471
00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:14.430
Hodor!

472
00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:46.830
Bran!

473
00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:52.800
Save yourself. now!

474
00:36:18.340 --> 00:36:20.240
Come with me. Brandon Stark.

475
00:36:27.680 --> 00:36:28.670
He is lost.

476
00:36:30.050 --> 00:36:31.990
Come with me or die with him.

477
00:36:33.050 --> 00:36:34.450
Go with them.

478
00:37:38.050 --> 00:37:39.750
They cannot follow us.

479
00:37:39.820 --> 00:37:42.050
The power that moves them is powerless here.

480
00:37:43.590 --> 00:37:45.060
Who are you?

481
00:37:45.130 --> 00:37:49.720
The First Men called us the Children.

482
00:37:45.130 --> 00:37:49.720
but we were born long before them.

483
00:37:50.100 --> 00:37:52.530
Come. he waits for you.

484
00:39:17.150 --> 00:39:19.380
You're the three-eyed raven?

485
00:39:23.420 --> 00:39:25.690
I've been many things.

486
00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:29.250
Now I am what you see.

487
00:39:31.200 --> 00:39:34.600
My brother. he led us to you and now he...

488
00:39:34.670 --> 00:39:36.970
He knew what would happen.

489
00:39:37.200 --> 00:39:39.500
From the moment he left.

490
00:39:39.610 --> 00:39:42.700
he knew and he went anyway.

491
00:39:42.780 --> 00:39:44.000
How do you know?

492
00:39:44.080 --> 00:39:45.980
I've been watching you.

493
00:39:46.580 --> 00:39:47.950
All of you.

494
00:39:48.410 --> 00:39:50.180
All of your lives.

495
00:39:50.780 --> 00:39:52.950
With 1.000 eyes and one.

496
00:39:55.420 --> 00:39:57.690
Now you've come to me at last.

497
00:39:57.760 --> 00:39:59.780
Brandon Stark.

498
00:40:00.990 --> 00:40:02.930
Though the hour is late.

499
00:40:03.800 --> 00:40:05.890
I didn't want anyone to die for me.

500
00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:09.330
He died so you could find what you have lost.

501
00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:13.500
You're going to help me walk again?

502
00:40:14.540 --> 00:40:17.070
You will never walk again.

503
00:40:19.280 --> 00:40:21.340
But you will fly.

504
00:40:37.360 --> 00:40:39.030
Podrick.

505
00:40:39.930 --> 00:40:41.870
Podrick.

506
00:40:41.940 --> 00:40:43.370
Where are the horses?

507
00:40:44.840 --> 00:40:46.770
I hobbled them last night.

508
00:40:46.840 --> 00:40:48.360
What sort of hobble?

509
00:40:48.440 --> 00:40:50.000
A figure eight. like you taught me.

510
00:40:51.180 --> 00:40:53.610
If you did it like I taught you.

511
00:40:51.180 --> 00:40:53.610
then the horses would be here.

512
00:40:53.680 --> 00:40:54.670
Thieves. maybe?

513
00:40:55.480 --> 00:40:58.380
It's at least 30 miles to the Eyrie from here.

514
00:40:58.720 --> 00:41:00.240
You're carrying the saddlebags.

515
00:41:28.650 --> 00:41:29.640
People coming.

516
00:41:32.090 --> 00:41:34.780
You can shit later. There's people coming.

517
00:41:37.160 --> 00:41:38.150
Morning.

518
00:41:40.460 --> 00:41:41.830
Morning.

519
00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:44.420
I like your sword.

520
00:41:46.230 --> 00:41:48.530
Are we getting close to the Bloody Gate?

521
00:41:49.400 --> 00:41:50.530
About 10 more miles.

522
00:41:50.940 --> 00:41:52.740
Did you hear that. Podrick?

523
00:41:52.810 --> 00:41:54.770
Only 10 more miles to the Bloody Gate.

524
00:41:57.110 --> 00:41:58.240
Are you a knight?

525
00:41:59.080 --> 00:42:00.240
No.

526
00:42:00.750 --> 00:42:02.480
But you know how to use that sword?

527
00:42:03.120 --> 00:42:04.580
I do.

528
00:42:05.920 --> 00:42:07.320
Does it have a name?

529
00:42:08.050 --> 00:42:09.650
Oathkeeper.

530
00:42:09.720 --> 00:42:11.120
Mine's Needle.

531
00:42:11.960 --> 00:42:13.360
Good name.

532
00:42:15.730 --> 00:42:17.360
Who taught you how to fight?

533
00:42:18.730 --> 00:42:20.060
My father.

534
00:42:22.070 --> 00:42:24.060
Mine never wanted to.

535
00:42:25.070 --> 00:42:27.400
Said fighting was for boys.

536
00:42:27.470 --> 00:42:29.470
Mine said the same.

537
00:42:29.940 --> 00:42:31.600
But I kept fighting the boys anyway.

538
00:42:32.550 --> 00:42:33.950
Kept losing.

539
00:42:34.010 --> 00:42:35.450
Finally my father said.

540
00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:38.080
"If you're going to do it.

541
00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:38.080
you might as well do it right."

542
00:42:42.560 --> 00:42:44.080
Seven blessings.

543
00:42:44.160 --> 00:42:46.460
I'm Brienne of Tarth. This is Podrick Payne.

544
00:42:49.360 --> 00:42:50.730
You want something?

545
00:42:51.260 --> 00:42:54.230
That's Sandor Clegane. The Hound.

546
00:43:05.410 --> 00:43:07.180
You're Arya Stark.

547
00:43:07.650 --> 00:43:10.210
I asked if you wanted something.

548
00:43:10.280 --> 00:43:12.880
I swore to your mother

549
00:43:10.280 --> 00:43:12.880
I would bring you home to her.

550
00:43:14.390 --> 00:43:17.050
- My mother's dead.

551
00:43:14.390 --> 00:43:17.050
- I know.

552
00:43:17.960 --> 00:43:20.120
I wish I could have been there to protect her.

553
00:43:21.630 --> 00:43:23.030
You're not a Northerner.

554
00:43:23.100 --> 00:43:26.330
No. but I swore a sacred vow to protect her.

555
00:43:27.470 --> 00:43:28.730
Why didn't you?

556
00:43:32.870 --> 00:43:35.640
She commanded me to bring

557
00:43:32.870 --> 00:43:35.640
Jaime Lannister back to King's Landing.

558
00:43:35.710 --> 00:43:37.440
You're paid by the Lannisters.

559
00:43:38.410 --> 00:43:40.040
You're here for the bounty on me.

560
00:43:41.380 --> 00:43:42.780
I'm not paid by the Lannisters.

561
00:43:42.850 --> 00:43:43.940
No?

562
00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:49.480
Fancy sword you've got there.

563
00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:49.480
Where'd you get it?

564
00:43:52.490 --> 00:43:54.890
I've been looking at Lannister gold all my life.

565
00:43:56.800 --> 00:43:59.600
Go on. Brienne of fucking Tarth.

566
00:43:59.670 --> 00:44:01.690
Tell me that's not Lannister gold.

567
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:05.870
Jaime Lannister gave me this sword.

568
00:44:06.370 --> 00:44:07.770
The Bloody Gate is 10 miles.

569
00:44:07.840 --> 00:44:09.600
I swore to your mother

570
00:44:07.840 --> 00:44:09.600
by the old gods and the new.

571
00:44:09.680 --> 00:44:11.080
I don't care what you swore.

572
00:44:11.140 --> 00:44:12.640
- Arya!

573
00:44:11.140 --> 00:44:12.640
- You heard the girl.

574
00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:15.480
- She's not coming with you.

575
00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:15.480
- She is.

576
00:44:17.780 --> 00:44:19.050
You're not a good listener.

577
00:44:19.750 --> 00:44:20.880
Valyrian steel?

578
00:44:22.090 --> 00:44:23.850
I always wanted some Valyrian steel.

579
00:44:23.920 --> 00:44:26.690
Come with me. Arya. I'll take you to safety.

580
00:44:26.760 --> 00:44:29.460
Safety? Where the fuck's that?

581
00:44:29.530 --> 00:44:30.720
Her aunt in the Eyrie is dead.

582
00:44:30.800 --> 00:44:33.730
Her mother's dead. Her father's dead.

583
00:44:30.800 --> 00:44:33.730
Her brother's dead.

584
00:44:33.800 --> 00:44:36.100
Winterfell is a pile of rubble.

585
00:44:36.170 --> 00:44:38.300
There is no safety. you dumb bitch.

586
00:44:39.770 --> 00:44:43.940
You don't know that by now.

587
00:44:39.770 --> 00:44:43.940
you're the wrong one to watch over her.

588
00:44:44.010 --> 00:44:46.340
And that's what you're doing?

589
00:44:46.410 --> 00:44:47.810
Watching over her?

590
00:44:49.080 --> 00:44:50.910
Aye. that's what I'm doing.

591
00:45:59.190 --> 00:46:01.050
I have no wish to kill you. Ser.

592
00:46:14.530 --> 00:46:15.590
I'm not a knight.

593
00:47:33.810 --> 00:47:35.780
Arya!

594
00:47:35.850 --> 00:47:37.710
Arya!

595
00:47:38.920 --> 00:47:40.750
Arya!

596
00:47:42.120 --> 00:47:44.490
- Where is she?

597
00:47:42.120 --> 00:47:44.490
- She was just here.

598
00:47:44.560 --> 00:47:45.650
Why weren't you watching her?

599
00:47:45.730 --> 00:47:47.660
I was watching you.

600
00:47:45.730 --> 00:47:47.660
I thought you might need some help.

601
00:47:47.730 --> 00:47:49.890
Which way. Pod? Which way did she go?

602
00:47:49.960 --> 00:47:51.860
I think that way.

603
00:47:51.930 --> 00:47:53.900
Arya!

604
00:47:53.970 --> 00:47:55.900
Arya!

605
00:48:24.660 --> 00:48:26.660
You still here?

606
00:48:36.780 --> 00:48:38.440
Big bitch saved you.

607
00:48:39.550 --> 00:48:40.980
I don't need saving.

608
00:48:41.050 --> 00:48:43.410
No. not you. You're a real killer.

609
00:48:43.550 --> 00:48:45.950
With your water dancing

610
00:48:46.020 --> 00:48:47.880
and your Needle.

611
00:48:49.090 --> 00:48:50.990
You gonna die?

612
00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:53.550
Unless there's a maester

613
00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:53.550
hiding behind that rock.

614
00:48:54.730 --> 00:48:56.030
aye.

615
00:48:56.900 --> 00:48:58.560
I'm done.

616
00:49:02.230 --> 00:49:03.900
I'd skin you alive for wine.

617
00:49:06.110 --> 00:49:07.970
Fuck water.

618
00:49:09.810 --> 00:49:11.970
Killed by a woman.

619
00:49:13.680 --> 00:49:14.810
I bet you like that.

620
00:49:17.750 --> 00:49:19.340
Go on.

621
00:49:19.850 --> 00:49:21.450
go after her.

622
00:49:22.490 --> 00:49:23.980
She'll help you.

623
00:49:27.630 --> 00:49:29.250
Going it alone.

624
00:49:29.830 --> 00:49:32.230
you won't last a day out there.

625
00:49:32.900 --> 00:49:35.370
I'll last longer than you.

626
00:49:41.840 --> 00:49:44.400
You remember where the heart is?

627
00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:54.690
Fuck it. I'm ready.

628
00:49:57.490 --> 00:49:58.720
Go on. girl.

629
00:49:59.760 --> 00:50:02.130
Another name off your list.

630
00:50:02.860 --> 00:50:05.060
You kept promising me.

631
00:50:11.940 --> 00:50:16.030
I cut down your butcher's boy. The ginger.

632
00:50:17.680 --> 00:50:19.870
He was begging for mercy.

633
00:50:19.950 --> 00:50:22.940
"Please. Ser. Please don't kill me.

634
00:50:23.020 --> 00:50:24.980
"Please. please."

635
00:50:26.750 --> 00:50:29.480
Bled all over my horse.

636
00:50:29.560 --> 00:50:31.920
Saddle stunk of butcher's boy for weeks.

637
00:50:35.160 --> 00:50:36.920
And your sister.

638
00:50:37.960 --> 00:50:39.730
Your pretty sister.

639
00:50:41.070 --> 00:50:43.660
I should have taken her.

640
00:50:44.370 --> 00:50:47.070
That night the Blackwater burned.

641
00:50:48.470 --> 00:50:50.100
I should have fucked her bloody.

642
00:50:51.740 --> 00:50:54.370
At least I'd have one happy memory.

643
00:51:04.720 --> 00:51:06.780
Do I have to beg you?

644
00:51:11.500 --> 00:51:13.060
Do it.

645
00:51:18.170 --> 00:51:19.900
Do it.

646
00:51:23.140 --> 00:51:24.700
Do it.

647
00:51:54.740 --> 00:51:56.830
Kill me.

648
00:52:00.080 --> 00:52:01.100
Kill me!

649
00:52:04.220 --> 00:52:06.410
Kill me!

650
00:52:07.890 --> 00:52:08.880
Kill me!

651
00:52:19.570 --> 00:52:21.900
Get on with it. you son of a whore.

652
00:52:22.400 --> 00:52:24.060
Is that any way to speak about our mother?

653
00:52:25.400 --> 00:52:27.740
- What are you doing?

654
00:52:25.400 --> 00:52:27.740
- What do you think I'm doing?

655
00:52:27.810 --> 00:52:29.710
A galley's waiting in the bay

656
00:52:27.810 --> 00:52:29.710
bound for the Free Cities.

657
00:52:29.780 --> 00:52:31.240
- Who's helping you?

658
00:52:29.780 --> 00:52:31.240
- Varys.

659
00:52:31.310 --> 00:52:33.540
- Varys?

660
00:52:31.310 --> 00:52:33.540
- You have more friends than you thought.

661
00:52:45.260 --> 00:52:46.820
There's a locked door at the top of the stairs.

662
00:52:47.160 --> 00:52:49.250
Knock on it twice. then twice again.

663
00:52:50.530 --> 00:52:52.020
Varys will open.

664
00:52:52.830 --> 00:52:55.030
I suppose this is goodbye. then.

665
00:53:10.750 --> 00:53:12.780
Farewell. little brother.

666
00:53:14.150 --> 00:53:15.640
Jaime.

667
00:53:17.320 --> 00:53:20.260
Thank you. For my life.

668
00:53:23.330 --> 00:53:25.190
Quickly now.

669
00:54:44.380 --> 00:54:45.900
Tywin?

670
00:54:49.080 --> 00:54:50.110
My lion.

671
00:56:09.930 --> 00:56:11.330
I'm sorry.

672
00:56:24.640 --> 00:56:26.340
I'm sorry.

673
00:57:13.430 --> 00:57:15.260
Tyrion.

674
00:57:16.660 --> 00:57:17.860
Put down the crossbow.

675
00:57:22.100 --> 00:57:23.690
Who released you?

676
00:57:25.570 --> 00:57:28.540
Your brother. I expect.

677
00:57:25.570 --> 00:57:28.540
He always had a soft spot for you.

678
00:57:29.880 --> 00:57:32.370
Come. we'll go and talk in my chambers.

679
00:57:37.020 --> 00:57:40.010
This is how you want to speak to me?

680
00:57:40.090 --> 00:57:42.380
Shaming your father has

681
00:57:40.090 --> 00:57:42.380
always given you pleasure...

682
00:57:42.450 --> 00:57:44.320
All my life

683
00:57:44.390 --> 00:57:46.520
you've wanted me dead.

684
00:57:49.430 --> 00:57:50.490
Yes.

685
00:57:51.330 --> 00:57:53.200
But you refused to die.

686
00:57:53.270 --> 00:57:54.730
I respect that.

687
00:57:55.570 --> 00:57:56.630
Even admire it.

688
00:57:56.940 --> 00:57:59.000
You fight for what's yours.

689
00:57:59.670 --> 00:58:02.700
I'd never let them execute you.

690
00:57:59.670 --> 00:58:02.700
Is that what you fear?

691
00:58:03.210 --> 00:58:05.680
I'll never let Ilyn Payne take your head.

692
00:58:05.740 --> 00:58:07.770
You're a Lannister.

693
00:58:10.120 --> 00:58:12.050
You're my son.

694
00:58:14.550 --> 00:58:15.820
I loved her.

695
00:58:16.620 --> 00:58:17.850
Who?

696
00:58:18.860 --> 00:58:20.290
Shae.

697
00:58:20.990 --> 00:58:22.390
Tyrion.

698
00:58:23.730 --> 00:58:24.720
Put down that crossbow.

699
00:58:24.800 --> 00:58:26.030
I murdered her.

700
00:58:28.570 --> 00:58:30.200
With my own hands.

701
00:58:33.570 --> 00:58:34.600
It doesn't matter.

702
00:58:35.010 --> 00:58:36.770
Doesn't matter?

703
00:58:37.140 --> 00:58:38.170
She was a whore.

704
00:58:40.850 --> 00:58:42.870
- Say that word again...

705
00:58:40.850 --> 00:58:42.870
- And what?

706
00:58:42.950 --> 00:58:45.350
You'll kill your own father in the privy?

707
00:58:46.850 --> 00:58:48.010
No.

708
00:58:48.920 --> 00:58:50.050
You're my son.

709
00:58:50.990 --> 00:58:52.510
Now. enough of this nonsense.

710
00:58:52.590 --> 00:58:55.890
I am your son. and you sentenced me to die.

711
00:58:56.260 --> 00:58:59.790
You knew I didn't poison Joffrey.

712
00:58:59.870 --> 00:59:02.630
but you sentenced me all the same.

713
00:59:03.170 --> 00:59:05.160
- Why?

714
00:59:03.170 --> 00:59:05.160
- Enough.

715
00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:08.270
We'll go back to my chambers

716
00:59:05.500 --> 00:59:08.270
and speak with some dignity.

717
00:59:08.340 --> 00:59:11.000
I can't go back there. She's in there.

718
00:59:11.080 --> 00:59:12.100
You're afraid of a dead whore?

719
00:59:25.490 --> 00:59:26.860
You shot me.

720
00:59:36.330 --> 00:59:38.200
You're no son of mine.

721
00:59:38.270 --> 00:59:39.530
I am your son.

722
00:59:41.470 --> 00:59:43.670
I have always been your son.

723
00:59:58.590 --> 01:00:00.460
What have you done?

724
01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:03.620
Quickly.

725
01:00:07.030 --> 01:00:10.060
Trust me. my friend. I've brought you this far.

726
01:02:05.050 --> 01:02:06.680
I want to see the captain.

727
01:02:06.750 --> 01:02:08.480
You're seeing him.

728
01:02:08.550 --> 01:02:10.680
I want to go north. to the Wall.

729
01:02:11.620 --> 01:02:13.110
No. you don't.

730
01:02:14.060 --> 01:02:15.430
I can pay.

731
01:02:15.490 --> 01:02:18.550
There is nothing in the North

732
01:02:15.490 --> 01:02:18.550
but ice and war and pirates.

733
01:02:18.630 --> 01:02:21.830
I wouldn't need a cabin. Please.

734
01:02:21.900 --> 01:02:23.560
I could work scrubbing the floors...

735
01:02:23.640 --> 01:02:26.430
I'm not going north. child. I'm going home.

736
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:29.370
- Where's home?

737
01:02:26.500 --> 01:02:29.370
- The Free City of Braavos.

738
01:02:30.680 --> 01:02:32.230
Wait. I have something else.

739
01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:35.910
- More silver won't make a difference.

740
01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:35.910
- It's not silver.

741
01:02:35.980 --> 01:02:37.140
It's iron.

742
01:02:40.050 --> 01:02:41.420
This...

743
01:02:45.690 --> 01:02:48.180
- How did you...

744
01:02:45.690 --> 01:02:48.180
- Valar Morghulis.

745
01:02:50.760 --> 01:02:52.660
Valar Dohaeris.

746
01:02:52.730 --> 01:02:55.430
Of course. you shall have a cabin.
